    "title": "Green vs Daniels - News, Tape, Ringwalk, TV, Streaming & Tickets",
    "text": "Who won Green vs Daniels? Lani Daniels beat Shadasia Green by technical knockout in the 9th round on Friday, April 17th, 2026, at Madison Square Garden Theater, New York. The fight was scheduled to take place over 10 rounds in the Super Middleweight division, which meant the weight limit was 168 pounds (12 stone or 76.2 kg). This fight appeared on the undercard of Alycia Baumgardner's and Bo Mi Re Shin's clash. Green vs Daniels stats Shadasia Green stepped into the ring with a record of 16 wins, 1 loss, and 0 draws, 11 of those wins coming by way of knockout. Lani Daniels made her way to the ring with a record of 11 wins, 4 losses and 2 draws, with 1 of those wins by knockout. The stats suggested Green had a massive power advantage over Daniels, boasting a 69% knockout percentage compared to Daniels' 9%. Shadasia Green was the younger woman by 1 year, at 36 years old. Green had a height advantage of 1 inch over Daniels. That also extended to a 1-inch reach advantage. Both Shadasia Green and Lani Daniels fought out of an orthodox stance. Green was the less experienced professional fighter, having had the same amount of fights, and made her debut in 2019, 1 year and 4 months later than Daniels, whose first professional fight was in 2017. She had fought 56 fewer professional rounds, totaling 93 compared to Daniels' 149. Green vs Daniels form Shadasia Green had beaten 4 of her last 5 opponents. In her last fight leading up to this contest, she had defeated Savannah Marshall on July 11, 2025, by split decision in their 10 round contest at Madison Square Garden, New York, United States. Prior to that, she had defeated Melinda Watpool on November 15, 2024, by split decision in their 10 round contest at AT&T Stadium, Arlington. Going into that contest, she had beaten Natasha Spence on July 20, 2024, by unanimous decision in their 8 round contest at Amalie Arena, Tampa. Before that, she had been beaten by Franchon Crews Dezurn on December 15, 2023, by unanimous decision in their 10 round contest at Caribe Royale Resort, Orlando. She had won against Olivia Curry on August 5, 2023, by unanimous decision in their 10 round contest at American Airlines Center, Dallas. Activity check Green's last 5 fights had come over a period of 2 years, 8 months and 12 days, which means she had been fighting approximately every 6 months and 16 days. In those fights, she fought a total of 48 rounds, meaning that they had lasted 9.6 rounds on average. What time did Green vs Daniels start? The fighters were expected to ringwalk at around 10:00 PM EST / 7:00 PM PST at Madison Square Garden Theater, New York, United States, which was around 3:00 AM BST in the UK. Who broadcast Green vs Daniels? Green vs Daniels was broadcast on ESPN in the US, while the fight was broadcast in the United Kingdom by Sky Sports+. What were the odds on Green vs Daniels? Shadasia Green was a 1/7 (-710) favorite going into the contest, while Lani Daniels made her way into the ring at 27/5 (+560) with oddsmakers.",
